ulate the  speed and the distance of the object  that you're aiming at and its trajectory  you have to think about the trajectory  of the object you go throw make sure it  hits it when it lands there never think  about the weight of the object you need  to think about the wind the angle and  all of this in a fraction of a second we  actually use a part of our brain to  calculate all this that we don't  normally have access to for performing  regular maths and there is a guy who can  use that part of the brain and he can do  it in such a way that you perform sums  quicker than a calculator and of course  I'll be talking about that in future  videos and on the website so there's a  bunch of ways you can train a little bit  more like aeronaut I need to develop the  body of arrow but also is explosive  strength and speed and potentially his  aiming skills as well and the last thing  to consider is how you're gonna fit all  this into your regular training program  because most of us don't have time on  top of everything else we do to do  near-far drills or to track objects with  the rise or to train our grip or our  lats and my answer to that is I've  talked about in the Batman training  video to have a skills workout this is  one day out of your regular workout that  it focuses on all their cool skills that  you don't have time for in the regular  splits that means things like  flexibility or  rip strength orale so that's when you  can do those kinds of things like the  near-far drill and develop really cool  skills that will give you the edge over  everyone else in the gym so this make  sense to me because it fits my training  philosophy which is GPD which stands for  general preparedness training basically  being ready for anything and if that's  the kind of training that appeals to you  then follow some of this advice and you  should be right on target  that was cringe  so thanks ton for watching guys hope you  found this video useful and interesting  if you did then